WEBVTT

00:00:08.610 --> 00:00:11.790
arashi no naka de kagayaite
You see the dream shining within the storm.

00:00:11.790 --> 00:00:16.080
sono yume o akiramenaide
Hang on to it now! Don't let it go.

00:00:16.150 --> 00:00:19.640
kizutsuita anata no senaka no
All I want is to take those wings on your back...

00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:23.890
tenshi no hane sotto daite
Those wounded angel wings, and gently...

00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:27.490
daite agetai
...pull them close to me.

00:00:33.570 --> 00:00:39.800
aoku hatenai sora no katasumi de
Newborn in a corner of the endless blue sky...

00:00:39.880 --> 00:00:43.080
umareta yume ga
The dream is there,

00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:46.210
ima chiisakutemo
and even though it may now be small...

00:00:47.350 --> 00:00:51.080
koori tsuku you na
No matter how strong they may blow...

00:00:51.150 --> 00:00:55.060
tsuyoi kaze de sae
...or how icy they may be...

00:00:55.120 --> 00:00:58.830
sono mune ni kagayaku
...those winds can never erase...

00:00:58.830 --> 00:01:03.260
yume o keshitari, sou yo
...the dream that shines. Oh, no!

00:01:03.330 --> 00:01:06.770
keshitari nante dekinai
The dream that shines inside your heart!

00:01:06.870 --> 00:01:10.000
arashi no naka de kagayaite
You see the dream shining within the storm.

00:01:10.070 --> 00:01:14.200
sono yume o akiramenaide
Hang on to it now! Don't let it go.

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:17.800
kizutsuita anata no senaka no
All I want is to take those wings on your back...

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:22.040
tenshi no hane sotto daite
Those wounded angel wings, and gently...

00:01:22.120 --> 00:01:26.420
daite agetai
...pull them close to me.

00:01:44.770 --> 00:01:47.310
God, what a smell!
All these trees!

00:01:47.380 --> 00:01:48.880
Yeah.

00:01:49.070 --> 00:01:51.630
The Earth can be
really nasty, can't it?

00:01:51.710 --> 00:01:53.360
You'll get used to it.

00:01:53.430 --> 00:01:56.620
Different from those air-
conditioned colonies, huh?

00:01:57.050 --> 00:02:00.050
Um, what was your
name again, Master Chief?

00:02:00.710 --> 00:02:03.240
Master Chief Petty Officer
Karen Joshua, sir!

00:02:04.920 --> 00:02:07.650
Gotcha.
Master Chief Karen Joshua.

00:02:07.820 --> 00:02:10.220
You been stationed here long?

00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:14.000
For 3 months, sir.
What about it?

00:02:14.330 --> 00:02:19.020
Nothing. Just curious.
Anyway, pleased to meet you.

00:02:19.090 --> 00:02:20.470
Same here.

00:02:24.450 --> 00:02:25.770
Mobile suits!

00:02:30.100 --> 00:02:31.440
They're loaded for land battle!

00:02:36.490 --> 00:02:39.150
Can I get one of
those, too?! Cool!

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:49.950
Ensign Shiro Amada
reporting for duty...

00:02:49.950 --> 00:02:51.930
...in the 08th mobile
suit team, sir!

00:02:52.070 --> 00:02:55.000
Welcome.
I'm battalion commander Kojima.

00:02:56.370 --> 00:02:57.330
Please, take it easy.

00:02:58.770 --> 00:03:02.750
God, I really hate air-
conditioning, you know?

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:05.510
That's why I usually retreat
out here during the day.

00:03:06.100 --> 00:03:09.510
That officer? I hear he went
after the Zeeks in a Ball.

00:03:09.790 --> 00:03:12.930
Still, I can't believe the Team
Killer is part of his group.

00:03:13.620 --> 00:03:16.270
I'm sure you've all
heard the reports...

00:03:16.270 --> 00:03:19.350
...that the Zeon have established
a secret factory in this area.

00:03:20.630 --> 00:03:24.120
However, what they're doing
there remains a mystery.

00:03:25.030 --> 00:03:28.200
And due to the fact that
their final defense line...

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:32.270
...is moving into our area,
we've decided to make our move.

00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:36.460
No matter what, we have to
break that defense line...

00:03:37.080 --> 00:03:39.070
...and hit the enemy hard!

00:03:44.730 --> 00:03:47.220
So, which one's
Sanders the Reaper?

00:03:47.420 --> 00:03:50.210
Quit asking questions.
You'll just get in trouble.

00:03:51.850 --> 00:03:55.720
Oh, and there are civilians
in the jungle as well.

00:03:56.560 --> 00:03:58.470
Try not to stir them up.

00:03:58.840 --> 00:04:01.010
Anyway, that's that.

00:04:01.420 --> 00:04:04.430
If there's anything else,
ask the master chief. Okay, Karen?

00:04:04.770 --> 00:04:05.360
Sir!

00:04:06.450 --> 00:04:08.430
C'mon, move aside!
Make a hole!

00:04:08.980 --> 00:04:11.100
Looks like the new
commander's arrived.

00:04:11.370 --> 00:04:12.790
Yeah, pretty much.

00:04:15.180 --> 00:04:17.010
So, what's he like?

00:04:17.650 --> 00:04:18.900
An unknown quantity
at the moment.

00:04:20.250 --> 00:04:22.380
Looks like you guys'll
be busy from now on.

00:04:22.990 --> 00:04:24.340
...and that's basically
the situation.

00:04:25.620 --> 00:04:26.990
How about it, Pops?

00:04:27.160 --> 00:04:30.260
Wanna bet how long he'll last?
The new commander.

00:04:32.180 --> 00:04:34.010
Give the guy a chance,
you damn fool!

00:04:36.340 --> 00:04:38.030
Okay, you're on!

00:04:40.980 --> 00:04:43.170
We're going out to
back up the 06th Team!

00:04:43.240 --> 00:04:45.940
Gimme a weapons and ammo check
and shake a leg on reloading!

00:04:46.010 --> 00:04:47.850
Chief Sanders! You're in Unit 3!

00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:48.600
Right!

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:52.680
Listen, the Zeeks aren't gonna
come visit us when it's convenient.

00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:57.090
Pull that camo netting
off of Units 1 and 3!

00:04:57.120 --> 00:04:57.760
Aye, aye!

00:04:57.980 --> 00:04:59.810
She is <i>so</i> cool.

00:05:02.310 --> 00:05:04.610
Excuse me.
Where's <i>my</i> mobile suit?

00:05:05.490 --> 00:05:07.750
You're my support man, kid.

00:05:09.400 --> 00:05:11.460
You handle the gun on
that as my assistant.

00:05:11.630 --> 00:05:13.610
HUH?! Assistant?

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:19.640
Don't catch that
on the gun barrel!

00:05:19.790 --> 00:05:22.600
Unit 3's loaded
with 100 millimeter!

00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:24.280
Cartridges are set, also!

00:05:24.350 --> 00:05:25.180
Okay!

00:05:25.410 --> 00:05:26.910
This is it...

00:05:29.400 --> 00:05:31.190
This is my mobile suit.

00:05:42.800 --> 00:05:44.330
Anything wrong, sir?

00:05:45.930 --> 00:05:46.930
Oh, no.

00:05:47.030 --> 00:05:49.330
It's in excellent condition,
Master Chief Joshua.

00:05:49.710 --> 00:05:51.040
I'm honored, sir!

00:06:33.610 --> 00:06:35.560
And now, before we move out...

00:06:35.560 --> 00:06:38.250
...our commander has something
he'd like to say to you.

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:46.720
I'm sorry I haven't had more of
a chance to get to know you all.

00:06:50.420 --> 00:06:53.380
I'll just say this: Whatever
happens, don't get killed.

00:06:53.750 --> 00:06:56.870
I'll also be doing whatever
it takes to see you don't die.

00:06:57.980 --> 00:07:00.410
No matter how heroic
you might be in a fight...

00:07:00.710 --> 00:07:02.900
...it doesn't mean anything
if you end up dying.

00:07:03.250 --> 00:07:05.190
As your commander,
it's my job to see...

00:07:05.200 --> 00:07:07.040
...that everyone in this
unit makes it back alive.

00:07:07.290 --> 00:07:10.980
It's my hope that we can all enjoy
victory together when it comes.

00:07:11.760 --> 00:07:12.980
That is all!

00:07:13.110 --> 00:07:16.080
All hands, prepare to
move out! Dismissed!

00:07:21.340 --> 00:07:22.940
<i>Well, he talks the talk...</i>

00:07:24.840 --> 00:07:27.760
Now, care to show us how
good you actually are?

00:07:28.190 --> 00:07:30.640
Show me a man who
<i>wants</i> to go and die!

00:07:30.710 --> 00:07:33.580
You're disappointing me,
Commander Newbie.

00:07:33.730 --> 00:07:35.450
But we know he's
a good pilot!

00:07:36.260 --> 00:07:37.560
We're about to find that out!

00:07:42.590 --> 00:07:45.710
I hope we make it
back alive. ALL of us...

00:08:01.020 --> 00:08:05.150
Sanders, you're on my right.
Joshua, take left wing.

00:08:05.780 --> 00:08:06.770
I'll take point.

00:08:07.650 --> 00:08:08.480
<i>Roger!</i>

00:08:08.550 --> 00:08:10.110
<i>08th Team, move out!</i>

00:08:36.040 --> 00:08:37.400
- <i>Commander?</i>
- What?

00:08:37.980 --> 00:08:40.280
We're about to leave
our defense line.

00:08:40.350 --> 00:08:42.340
From here on, no radio
transmissions are allowed.

00:08:42.420 --> 00:08:43.680
I'm aware of that.

00:08:43.750 --> 00:08:46.580
<i>All communications from here</i>
<i>on are to be pointcast only!</i>

00:08:47.490 --> 00:08:48.920
<i>Kill all lights!</i>

00:08:48.990 --> 00:08:51.460
<i>Switch over to laser sensors</i>
<i>and IR on your monitors!</i>

00:08:53.090 --> 00:08:55.360
We'll see how long
he can keep this act up...

00:08:59.970 --> 00:09:01.220
It's close!

00:09:02.970 --> 00:09:04.560
Kid, get Newbie on the line.

00:09:04.640 --> 00:09:07.110
- R- Right!
- And don't make a sound!

00:09:20.990 --> 00:09:26.220
Bearing to 2 o'clock...
Range: 2300. Two mobile suits.

00:09:27.130 --> 00:09:28.040
Can you ID them?

00:09:28.600 --> 00:09:29.990
Checking their profile...

00:09:32.420 --> 00:09:32.970
Zakus!

00:09:33.840 --> 00:09:35.340
What about the 06th Team?

00:09:35.840 --> 00:09:37.640
You think they were wiped out?

00:09:37.740 --> 00:09:39.930
<i>The enemy's still attacking.</i>

00:09:40.610 --> 00:09:41.940
They wouldn't be
if they were wiped out.

00:09:42.910 --> 00:09:43.930
Yeah, you're right.

00:09:44.610 --> 00:09:45.640
I'll go and check it out!

00:09:47.820 --> 00:09:49.620
Wants to play decoy, huh?

00:09:50.070 --> 00:09:51.870
But are you good
enough to do that?

00:10:08.240 --> 00:10:09.030
Here it comes!

00:10:15.100 --> 00:10:17.100
Uh-oh! This isn't like space!

00:10:19.290 --> 00:10:21.420
Trying to get killed
right after you got here?!

00:10:24.440 --> 00:10:25.260
Heavy!

00:10:31.790 --> 00:10:32.610
Kill your light!

00:10:33.560 --> 00:10:36.500
Master Chief Joshua!
What are you trying to do?!

00:10:36.560 --> 00:10:37.380
<i>It's no good!</i>

00:10:37.930 --> 00:10:40.320
I'm saying your piloting skill
isn't up to this situation!

00:10:40.600 --> 00:10:43.400
What?! Are you trying
to insult me?!

00:10:43.740 --> 00:10:45.620
<i>I don't care how you take it!</i>

00:10:49.590 --> 00:10:52.530
I'll stop that guy!
Just watch!

00:10:56.520 --> 00:10:59.880
I'm not good enough to take on
the enemy, huh? Well, fine!

00:11:01.870 --> 00:11:06.700
Newbie's following the Zaku.
Karen's on the commander's ass.

00:11:06.960 --> 00:11:08.260
Message from the commander!

00:11:08.330 --> 00:11:11.820
He says he's going after the Zaku
to drive it out of our defense line!

00:11:11.930 --> 00:11:14.560
Oh, that's just great.
This whole thing's totally FUBAR!

00:11:15.270 --> 00:11:17.200
- Get the Chief on the line!
- Right!

00:11:43.230 --> 00:11:44.960
Thought he said
there were two Zakus.

00:11:48.170 --> 00:11:48.980
Commander!

00:11:51.770 --> 00:11:52.770
He's in too close!

00:12:07.520 --> 00:12:08.490
Chief Sanders!

00:12:10.990 --> 00:12:13.060
This doesn't handle
like a GM at all!

00:12:17.330 --> 00:12:19.270
So, this is what a Gundam's like...

00:12:23.090 --> 00:12:24.160
Where is he?!

00:12:25.970 --> 00:12:28.070
Commander! Don't move in
too deep! It's dangerous!

00:12:31.240 --> 00:12:31.840
There he is!

00:12:35.880 --> 00:12:37.710
You see? I got him!

00:12:41.120 --> 00:12:42.300
Damn!

00:12:44.270 --> 00:12:45.070
Shit!

00:12:52.300 --> 00:12:53.790
Where'd he go?!

00:12:58.570 --> 00:13:00.270
What a mess!

00:13:07.110 --> 00:13:09.350
Eledore!
Has the commander come back yet?

00:13:09.830 --> 00:13:11.270
<i>Huh? I thought he was with you.</i>

00:13:11.490 --> 00:13:13.370
What are you
waiting for, Ninorich?!

00:13:14.170 --> 00:13:15.770
Hurry up and
find the commander!

00:13:16.190 --> 00:13:17.480
Y- Yes, ma'am!

00:13:17.630 --> 00:13:21.790
Commander! Ensign Amada!
Please respond on 3754!

00:13:23.540 --> 00:13:25.450
Maybe he's out taking a piss.

00:13:33.000 --> 00:13:36.700
Dammit! Where? Where'd he go?!

00:13:40.430 --> 00:13:42.650
Looks like he's out
of detection range.

00:13:42.760 --> 00:13:44.820
Should we send a rescue
team out after him?

00:13:44.980 --> 00:13:46.010
Are you stupid?

00:13:46.280 --> 00:13:49.180
If you do that so soon
after he gets here...

00:13:49.260 --> 00:13:51.220
...he'll be the laughingstock
of the base.

00:13:56.090 --> 00:13:57.290
<i>Commander...</i>

00:14:02.460 --> 00:14:05.530
Oh, great! The navigation
system's screwed up!

00:14:09.110 --> 00:14:10.270
God dammit!

00:14:10.710 --> 00:14:12.840
Oh, that's just great...

00:14:21.040 --> 00:14:23.910
If he's alive, he could at
least broadcast a mayday...

00:14:37.340 --> 00:14:40.030
If I stay in this thing,
I'll drown in my own sweat!

00:14:47.010 --> 00:14:49.740
God DAMN, it's hot!

00:14:53.850 --> 00:14:58.350
It's barely dawn, but it's
already so damn hot!

00:15:04.970 --> 00:15:07.760
Lovely. Just lovely.

00:15:11.510 --> 00:15:13.500
What the hell are these?!

00:15:25.520 --> 00:15:26.600
What's <i>with</i> this place?!

00:15:28.830 --> 00:15:31.480
And there are people
who actually <i>live</i> here?!

00:15:31.590 --> 00:15:33.030
I don't believe it.

00:15:34.530 --> 00:15:38.490
I get an insubordinate master chief
and a smart-ass petty officer!

00:15:59.520 --> 00:16:01.230
That's the stuff!

00:16:07.720 --> 00:16:09.040
I feel alive again!

00:16:35.360 --> 00:16:39.020
A...A girl? Yeah, it is.

00:16:46.430 --> 00:16:47.900
She's pretty.

00:16:50.640 --> 00:16:52.860
I heard about that battle
you were in 2 days ago.

00:16:53.070 --> 00:16:53.500
Yes.

00:16:53.870 --> 00:16:57.200
I heard the test unit was lost...
Why did you do it?

00:16:57.650 --> 00:17:00.570
One thing led to another.
Besides that...

00:17:02.100 --> 00:17:03.680
My Apsalus, you mean?

00:17:03.810 --> 00:17:04.370
Yes.

00:17:06.340 --> 00:17:08.610
The prototype should
be completed shortly.

00:17:10.410 --> 00:17:13.730
Then soon it'll be reality.
Your dream, Big Brother.

00:17:14.760 --> 00:17:19.670
No, it's not a dream anymore.
Once it's on the front line...

00:17:19.680 --> 00:17:22.070
...it will change the war
situation back to our favor.

00:17:22.140 --> 00:17:25.830
I heard Commandant Giren's
speech on my way here.

00:17:26.540 --> 00:17:29.130
I want to help you any
way I can, Big Brother.

00:17:31.290 --> 00:17:33.750
Now that you're here,
I feel more confident.

00:17:34.130 --> 00:17:38.380
Uh-oh. Big Brother, isn't
it time for your medicine?

00:17:39.040 --> 00:17:39.630
Right.

00:17:47.510 --> 00:17:49.230
There it goes again!

00:17:55.940 --> 00:17:58.220
Um...Gee!
I was just, uh!

00:18:02.030 --> 00:18:03.940
Cut it out! Don't shoot!

00:18:04.610 --> 00:18:06.350
He's a Fed pilot?

00:18:11.720 --> 00:18:13.710
She didn't have to just
start shooting at me!

00:18:19.010 --> 00:18:20.370
That guy from last night!

00:18:21.300 --> 00:18:23.730
He's wandering around
over there! All right, then!

00:18:33.050 --> 00:18:37.310
<i>Chief. Our relief is here.</i>
<i>Do we wait any longer?</i>

00:18:38.000 --> 00:18:40.090
We can't move until we get
orders from the commander.

00:18:41.050 --> 00:18:42.950
Not the most
flexible guy, are you?

00:18:43.020 --> 00:18:45.260
<i>I have a personal debt to him.</i>

00:18:46.720 --> 00:18:49.280
So, you're the team killer,
Sanders the Reaper.

00:18:49.660 --> 00:18:50.310
What?!

00:18:50.800 --> 00:18:53.070
I looked at your record before.

00:18:53.600 --> 00:18:55.860
You've shot down 6 enemy
suits with your GM.

00:18:56.840 --> 00:18:59.930
<i>If your luck was different,</i>
<i>you might be an officer now.</i>

00:19:00.330 --> 00:19:03.750
<i>But I've got the higher rank here,</i>
<i>so I'll give the orders.</i>

00:19:04.070 --> 00:19:04.610
But!

00:19:04.990 --> 00:19:07.400
The commander said we were
to go back alive, right?

00:19:07.610 --> 00:19:08.830
So we're going back!

00:19:16.010 --> 00:19:18.920
One strike...I'll stop
you with one strike.

00:19:19.810 --> 00:19:21.250
Now come and get me!

00:19:26.360 --> 00:19:29.200
Calm down.
Just calm down, Shiro.

00:19:32.260 --> 00:19:35.100
Even clumsy pilots have
clumsy ways of fighting.

00:19:35.360 --> 00:19:37.540
Now hurry up and get
into my firing range!

00:19:38.320 --> 00:19:38.920
Here he comes!

00:19:43.680 --> 00:19:46.830
I'll show you I've got the guts
for this, Joshua! Just watch!

00:19:49.450 --> 00:19:51.300
Even I can do this!

00:20:18.340 --> 00:20:19.410
He still wants to fight?!

00:20:59.690 --> 00:21:02.420
I did it, didn't I?
Even here on the ground.

00:21:08.890 --> 00:21:11.630
One kill down!
Now I can go home!

00:21:20.150 --> 00:21:21.350
Hey, Karen!

00:21:22.150 --> 00:21:23.840
Did this guy only last one day?

00:21:23.950 --> 00:21:25.340
Shouldn't have been
so rough on him!

00:21:25.710 --> 00:21:27.940
Or maybe he was just cursed!

00:21:33.080 --> 00:21:36.150
<i>B.B., I've barely</i>
<i>landed here on Earth...</i>

00:21:36.150 --> 00:21:38.710
<i>...and already I've had</i>
<i>my first taste of battle!</i>

00:21:38.790 --> 00:21:41.160
<i>I wish you could</i>
<i>have seen me fighting.</i>

00:21:41.730 --> 00:21:44.060
<i>But something really</i>
<i>awful happened out there.</i>

00:21:45.300 --> 00:21:48.200
<i>Our commander got separated</i>
<i>from us and never came back.</i>

00:21:49.100 --> 00:21:52.270
<i>The Earth can</i>
<i>be a harsh place.</i>

00:21:52.340 --> 00:21:54.400
<i>I wonder if I'm really</i>
<i>gonna get through this alive...</i>

00:21:54.510 --> 00:21:56.140
Hey, kid!

00:21:56.410 --> 00:21:58.310
He's come back!
Newbie's back!

00:22:07.050 --> 00:22:08.070
Commander!

00:22:08.490 --> 00:22:10.120
Christ, I don't believe it.

00:22:10.620 --> 00:22:11.890
He was like that
in space, too.

00:22:12.130 --> 00:22:14.490
Feel like taking a
chance on his luck, now?

00:22:17.060 --> 00:22:19.400
I'm thankful that mobile
suit's as good as it is.

00:22:31.780 --> 00:22:33.440
Enough already...

00:22:52.240 --> 00:22:54.980
osanaikoro kara
All that time that's passed me by.

00:22:55.050 --> 00:22:58.670
sou kyou made no so many days
From childhood till now, so many days.

00:22:58.750 --> 00:23:02.810
furikaereba ironna
When I look back, I see so many things...

00:23:02.890 --> 00:23:06.580
koto ni meguriatta
...that happened to come into my life.

00:23:06.660 --> 00:23:09.750
naitari warattari
The times I cried, the times I laughed.

00:23:10.060 --> 00:23:13.760
kenka shitari yume mitari
The times I fought, the times I dreamed.

00:23:13.830 --> 00:23:17.890
chotto hard na shitsuren mo
The lost loves that were sort of hard.

00:23:17.970 --> 00:23:21.030
kagayaku my history
All shining in my history.

00:23:21.710 --> 00:23:24.170
ikutsumono
The ones who caused me pain...

00:23:24.240 --> 00:23:29.040
deai to wakare kugurinukete
...I met and left along the way.

00:23:29.380 --> 00:23:34.910
ai suru anata ni sou yo
But I still ended up meeting you.

00:23:34.990 --> 00:23:39.250
Love! meguriaeta
The one that I love.

00:23:40.690 --> 00:23:44.150
Ten years after juunen go no
Ten years after, A decade from now.

00:23:44.260 --> 00:23:47.920
watashi wa doushiteru darou
I wonder what I will be doing then.

00:23:48.000 --> 00:23:55.060
donna fuu ni anata o sukideiru darou
I wonder how I will be still loving you.

00:23:55.840 --> 00:23:59.170
Ten years after, juunen go no
Ten years after, a decade from now.

00:23:59.240 --> 00:24:03.240
anata o mitsumete mitai
I still want to be looking at you.

00:24:03.310 --> 00:24:06.980
Stay together sono toki
Stay together. When that day comes...

00:24:07.050 --> 00:24:13.670
kitto soba de hohoendeitai
...I want to be at your side with a smile.

00:24:17.180 --> 00:24:18.880
Our new orders are handed down.

00:24:18.950 --> 00:24:22.250
We have to liberate a Zeon-
occupied village in the hills!

00:24:22.850 --> 00:24:24.320
To take out the enemy's
gun emplacements...

00:24:24.390 --> 00:24:26.720
...we split up to
try a pincer attack.

00:24:27.290 --> 00:24:30.390
But then I slip up and get
captured by guerrillas...

00:24:30.460 --> 00:24:32.790
...and the time to start the
attack is getting closer and closer!

00:24:32.860 --> 00:24:34.760
I can't let my
team die like dogs!

00:24:34.830 --> 00:24:36.960
Somehow, I've got to escape!

00:24:37.030 --> 00:24:41.330
Next time, on Mobile Suit Gundam -
The 08th MS Team:

00:24:41.410 --> 00:24:43.370
"The Time Limit on Trust."
